# Lesson 5, new exercise: partner invites with 2NT (no Stayman); student accepts.
title: Partner invites with 2NT
id: L05-24
type: exercise
lesson: 5
concepts: 5.6
student: S
board: 47
dealer: S
vulnerable: NS

deal:            # spades  hearts  diamonds  clubs
  N  J97    K5     J965   KJ87
  E  A82    Q62    Q843   QT3
  S  KQ3    JT43   AK7    A94
  W  T654   A987   T2     652

auction:
  S 1NT*   = 15-17 points, balanced
     not *: 17 points and a balanced hand: open 1NT.
  W Pass
  N 2NT    = 8-9 points, balanced, no 4-card major
  E Pass
  S 3NT*   = A maximum: accept
     key: Partner skipped Stayman, so there's no major fit. With 17, accept.
     not Pass: 17 is the top of your range. Accept the invitation.
     not 3H: Partner has no 4-card major, or she'd have used Stayman.
  W Pass
  N Pass
  E Pass

auction recap:
  Partner's 2NT is the old invitation: 8-9 points, and no 4-card major, since
  with one she'd have bid Stayman. Your four hearts don't matter. With a
  maximum you bid game. You are declarer, because you bid no-trump first, and
  so West will lead to the first trick.

planning:
  winners: 4
  remind: What is the contract? How many tricks do you need?

play:
  1   W S4  N S7  E S8  S SQ*
      SQ key: Win with the queen.
      SQ not S3: Did you notice your queen wins this trick? Take it while you can.
  2   S CA  W C2  N C7  E C3
      note: Start on clubs, your best chance for extra tricks.
  3   S C9*  W C5  N C8  E CT
      C9 key: Keep going with clubs. Giving up one trick sets up the rest.
      C9 not HJ: Did you count your winners? You need extra tricks from clubs, so keep playing them.
      C9 not DK: Did you count your winners? You need extra tricks from clubs, so keep playing them.
      note: You give up a club trick to set up the suit.
  4   E SA  S S3  W S5  N S9
  5   E S2  S SK  W S6  N SJ
  6   S HJ  W H7  N HK  E H2
      note: Lead the jack of hearts over to dummy's king.
  7   N CK  E CQ  S C4  W C6
      note: Cash the clubs you've set up.
  8   N CJ  E D4  S H3  W H8
      note: And the last good club.
  9   N DJ  E D8  S D7  W DT
      note: Try the jack of diamonds: if East has the queen and plays low, it wins.
  10  N D9  E DQ  S DK  W D2
      note: Over to your king of diamonds.
  11  S DA  W H9  N D5  E D3
      note: Cash the ♦A.
  12  S HT  W HA  N H5  E H6
      note: Lead a heart. The defense takes the rest.
  13  W ST  N D6  E HQ  S H4
      note: 9 tricks: 3NT made.

play recap:
  The plan: you start with only four sure tricks, so you have to build more.
  Give up a club to set up the suit, and drive out the ♠A.

  3NT made exactly. Partner's 8-9 plus your 17 was enough, and the old
  sequence did the job: no Stayman needed.
